# Catalog schema

## Site object

Required: `name`, `home_url`, `profile_url`, `check`, `profile`.

Optional: `probe_url`, `method` (GET only; omit or GET), `headers`,
`username_pattern`, `username_claimed`, `username_unclaimed`, `nsfw`.

`profile_url` / `probe_url` must include `{username}` where the username goes.

## Check types

| `check.type` | Behavior |
|--------------|----------|
| `status` | First response only (no follow). 2xx = found unless status in `not_found_status` (default 404) or soft-404 `not_found_text` matches body. Other codes (incl. 3xx) = unknown. |
| `body` | First response only. `not_found_text` substring => not found; else 2xx = found. |
| `redirect` | First response only. 2xx = found; otherwise not found. |

Unknown JSON fields are rejected (`DisallowUnknownFields`).

## Profiles and NSFW

Per-site `profile`: `default` | `developer` | `creative` | `community`.
CLI `-profile` may also use `full`. NSFW sites need `"nsfw": true` and `-nsfw` to include.

## Trust boundary (do not weaken)

Load rejects: non-`http`/`https`, private/link-local/metadata hosts, `POST`,
dangerous hop-by-hop / `Host` headers, invalid or over-long `username_pattern`.

## After edits

1. Rebuild so the embed updates: `go build -o social-gopher ./cmd/social-gopher`
2. For sites with claimed/unclaimed fixtures:
   `./social-gopher -validate-catalog -site <Name>`
